The trained neural network can output the momentum and quasipotential at the specified position. Since the lowest point of the quasipotential on the boundary is usually the saddle point. We start from the point near the saddle point to calculate the time-reverse integral of Eq. (2.10), where we use neural network calculation to get the momentum value. Eventually, we obtain the most probable path for the system to leave the attractive basin.
